# Copy this file to .env (same folder as app.json) if you want to turn
# on the optional CAPTCHA widget on the Signup and Forgot Password
# screens. Nothing here is required — the app builds and runs fully
# with zero config; the widget simply doesn't render (see
# src/components/Captcha.js), and the corresponding backend check
# no-ops too (see backend/.env.example's RECAPTCHA_SECRET_KEY).
#
# IMPORTANT: Expo only inlines env vars prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ into the
# app bundle (see EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL in src/services/api.js for
# the same convention already used elsewhere in this app) — anything
# else is invisible to process.env at runtime. Restart `npx expo
# start` after editing this file.

# The SAME site's key from google.com/recaptcha/admin that you used
# for RECAPTCHA_SECRET_KEY in backend/.env — this is the public "site
# key" half of that pair (safe to expose in app code; it identifies
# which site is asking, not a secret). See src/components/Captcha.js.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=
